/-!
# Principal kernel of a Cohen monoid presentation

Source: ILO, Travaux de Gabber, Exposé VI 1.6(ii), printed p. 70; the
agent refinement of the principal-kernel argument recorded in the DAG
(blueprint: lem-trf-cohen-monoid-surjection-principal-kernel).
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u v w

namespace AddMonoidAlgebra

/-- A surjective local Cohen monoid presentation of the expected dimension has
kernel generated by every relation `p - j` lifting `p` from the full boundary ideal.
The stratum equivalence is a coefficient-algebra equivalence fixing the parameters;
the quotient equivalence is the map induced by the given surjection on every element.

Source: ILO, Exposé VI 1.6(ii), printed p. 70, and the agent-refined argument
(blueprint: lem-trf-cohen-monoid-surjection-principal-kernel).

Proof:
1. `lem-weil-pbc-power-series-field-cohen-regular-complete` makes
   `D = C[[T₁,…,Tₙ]]` complete regular local of dimension `n+1`.
   `lem-trf-polynomial-power-series-monoid-completion` identifies the displayed
   completion with the formal monoid ring over `D`, fixes all generators and
   identifies its monomial quotient with `D`. Apply
   `lem-trf-formal-monoid-ring-dimension`: the completion is Noetherian local,
   a domain, and has dimension `n+1+r`.
2. The image of `p` in `D` is a nonunit, so `p` is a nonunit in the completion.
   Locality sends it into the maximal ideal of `S`, the image of `J`.
   Choose `j ∈ J` mapping to it. For any such `j`, `θ = p-j` lies in the kernel
   and `θ-p = -j ∈ J`. Its stratum image is congruent to `p` modulo the variables.
3. Constant coefficient sends the maximal ideal of `D` into `pC` and sends
   the stratum image of `θ` to `p`. If that image were in the square, then
   `p ∈ p²C`; cancellation in the Cohen domain would make `p` a unit.
   Thus the image lies in the maximal ideal but not its square.
4. The primitive-element clause of `lem-trf-formal-monoid-ring-dimension`
   gives dimension `n+r` for the hypersurface quotient.
   `lem-trf-log-regular-saturation-normality`, case (ii), makes it a nonzero
   domain since `θ-p ∈ J`. It is Noetherian local as a quotient by a proper ideal.
5. The surjection factors through this quotient. If its kernel were nonzero,
   pull back a prime chain of length `n+r` from `S` and prepend the zero prime.
   Surjectivity preserves strictness of the pulled-back inclusions; the first
   pulled-back prime is nonzero. This contradicts the quotient dimension `n+r`.
   Hence the induced kernel is zero and the original kernel is `(θ)`.
6. The induced bijection is a ring equivalence, with its specified formula on
   every element, hence on monomials and variables. A ring equivalence reflects
   units, so it is an isomorphism of local rings. No step depends on the choice
   of `j`. Empty monomial and variable generating families are allowed; when
   both are empty, `J=0`, `θ=p`, and the quotient is the residue field. -/
theorem cohenMonoidSurjection_principalKernel
    (C : Type u) [CommRing C] [IsLocalRing C] (p : ℕ) (hC : IsCohenRing p C)
    (P : Type v) [AddCommMonoid P]
    (hfs : AlgebraicGeometry.IsFineSaturatedMonoid (Multiplicative P))
    (hsharp : ∀ q : P, IsUnit (Multiplicative.ofAdd q) → q = 0)
    (n r : ℕ)
    (hr : r = Module.finrank ℚ (TensorProduct ℤ ℚ
      (Additive (Algebra.GrothendieckGroup (Multiplicative P)))))
    (N : Ideal (ToricMonoid.Complete C P n))
    (hN : N = Ideal.span {b | ∃ q : P, q ≠ 0 ∧ b =
      algebraMap (MvPolynomial (Fin n) (AddMonoidAlgebra C P)) (ToricMonoid.Complete C P n)
        (MvPolynomial.C (single q (1 : C)))})
    (S : Type w) [CommRing S] [IsNoetherianRing S] [IsLocalRing S]
    (hdim : ringKrullDim S = ((n + r : ℕ) : WithBot ℕ∞))
    (φ : ToricMonoid.Complete C P n →+* S) [IsLocalHom φ]
    (hφ : Function.Surjective φ)
    (hJ : Ideal.map φ (ToricMonoid.completedChartIdeal C P n) =
      IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal S) :
    (∃ j ∈ ToricMonoid.completedChartIdeal C P n,
      φ j = φ (p : ToricMonoid.Complete C P n)) ∧
    IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) C) =
      Ideal.span (insert (MvPowerSeries.C (p : C))
        (Set.range (MvPowerSeries.X : Fin n → MvPowerSeries (Fin n) C))) ∧
    ∃ e : (ToricMonoid.Complete C P n ⧸ N) ≃ₐ[C] MvPowerSeries (Fin n) C,
      (∀ i : Fin n, e (Ideal.Quotient.mk N
        (algebraMap (MvPolynomial (Fin n) (AddMonoidAlgebra C P)) (ToricMonoid.Complete C P n)
          (MvPolynomial.X i))) = MvPowerSeries.X i) ∧
      ∀ j ∈ ToricMonoid.completedChartIdeal C P n,
        φ j = φ (p : ToricMonoid.Complete C P n) →
        ((p : ToricMonoid.Complete C P n) - j) - p ∈
          ToricMonoid.completedChartIdeal C P n ∧
        RingHom.ker φ = Ideal.span {(p : ToricMonoid.Complete C P n) - j} ∧
        e (Ideal.Quotient.mk N ((p : ToricMonoid.Complete C P n) - j)) -
          MvPowerSeries.C (p : C) ∈
            Ideal.span (Set.range (MvPowerSeries.X : Fin n → MvPowerSeries (Fin n) C)) ∧
        e (Ideal.Quotient.mk N ((p : ToricMonoid.Complete C P n) - j)) ∈
          IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) C) ∧
        e (Ideal.Quotient.mk N ((p : ToricMonoid.Complete C P n) - j)) ∉
          (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) C)) ^ 2 ∧
        IsNoetherianRing
          (ToricMonoid.Complete C P n ⧸ Ideal.span {(p : ToricMonoid.Complete C P n) - j}) ∧
        IsLocalRing
          (ToricMonoid.Complete C P n ⧸ Ideal.span {(p : ToricMonoid.Complete C P n) - j}) ∧
        IsDomain
          (ToricMonoid.Complete C P n ⧸ Ideal.span {(p : ToricMonoid.Complete C P n) - j}) ∧
        ringKrullDim
          (ToricMonoid.Complete C P n ⧸ Ideal.span {(p : ToricMonoid.Complete C P n) - j}) =
            ((n + r : ℕ) : WithBot ℕ∞) ∧
        ∃ eS : (ToricMonoid.Complete C P n ⧸
            Ideal.span {(p : ToricMonoid.Complete C P n) - j}) ≃+* S,
          (∀ b : ToricMonoid.Complete C P n, eS (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ b) = φ b) ∧
          IsLocalHom eS.toRingHom := by
  sorry

end AddMonoidAlgebra
